// A LITERAL IN FN PARAMETER POSITION DELETES THE PARAMETER. `fn f(0)` is an
// arm on the argument that refuses every value but zero, so the fn is
// inexhaustive and must refuse with E_PatternInexhaustive (SYNTAX §«Refutable
// `let`»: a pattern in parameter position is an arm, never a hidden
// refusal). It refuses with E_TypeMismatch "Int vs ()" instead (measured
// 2026-09-25): the parameter list silently loses the literal, so `f` takes
// no arguments. The lambda form is mn-resolve-literal-param.
//
// Retires when a parameter is a pattern from its first token
// (Hβ.resolve.reference-is-an-edge, the binder landing).
fn f(0) = 1

fn main() = f(5)
